 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Non-intersection:** If $t_{min} > t_{max}$ or the ray origin is behind the box ($t_{max} < 0$), the ray does not intersect the node's bounding box. The algorithm returns an empty list [S1, unofficial].
-- **Precision:** Floating-point precision errors near the midpoint boundaries ($tx_m \approx t_{min}$) may lead to incorrect pruning [G]. It is recommended to use a small epsilon tolerance when comparing midpoint factors to $t_{min}$ and $t_{max}$ to avoid excluding valid children due to numerical noise.
-- **Child Indexing:** The specific set of children marked invalid depends on the octree's child indexing scheme. The source assumes a specific mapping where $\{1,2,3,4\}$ are on one side of the x-midplane and $\{5,6,7,8\}$ on the other. Implementers must verify their octree's indexing convention matches the sets used in the pruning rules [S1, unofficial].
